From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 Safe Browsing tab helpers for registry tabs (ABI 1.57)

Security audit RC-500 F-02, engine part. Bridge 0.60.0, feature
safe_browsing_tab_helpers. AttachBrowserlessTabHelpers attaches what
TabHelpers::AttachTabHelpers does for Safe Browsing, in its order:
ChromePasswordReuseDetectionManagerClient after the password manager client;
SafeBrowsingNavigationObserver (referrer chains), AsyncCheckTracker and
SafeBrowsingTabObserver (client-side phishing detection) after
PermissionRequestManager and the autofill client, which
ClientSideDetectionHost observes from its constructor; TriggerCreator;
SafetyTipWebContentsObserver (its bubble needs a Browser and is not shown).
ReArcEngineSafeBrowsingAvailable() is true only when Safe Browsing is compiled
in and google_apis::HasAPIKeyConfigured(): an engine built without a
google_api_key sends dummytoken, which Google rejects, so the host must not
claim protection.

Last rebased: 2026-11-10 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.96 (2ad9b7f5a8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

